	<system>

Supervisor = GCSSupervisor();

Sender0 = MissionSender(0);
Sender1 = MissionSender(1);
Sender2 = MissionSender(2);

Drone0 = MissionReceiver(0);
Drone1 = MissionReceiver(1);
Drone2 =MissionReceiver(2);

Link = Network();

// CommandClient and CommandServer are instantiated automatically
// for every drone_id: CommandClient(0), CommandClient(1), ...
system Supervisor,
       Sender0, Sender1, Sender2, Drone0, Drone1, Drone2, Link,
       CommandClient, CommandServer;</system>
	<queries>
		<query>
			<formula>A[] (Sender0.SendItem imply Drone0.WaitItem)</formula>
			<comment>(Jason, model 02) Mission: the GCS only sends an item when the drone waits for it.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>A[] (Drone0.RequestedItem imply
     Drone0.expectedCount == MISSION_SIZE)</formula>
			<comment>(Jason, model 02) HaveCount renamed RequestedItem: after the count, the drone expects MISSION_SIZE items.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>E&lt;&gt; (Sender0.SendItem &amp;&amp;
     Sender1.SendItem &amp;&amp;
     Sender2.SendItem)</formula>
			<comment>(Jason, model 02) The three uploads can run at the same time.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>E&lt;&gt; Supervisor.Prepared</formula>
			<comment>Every mission can be uploaded. Was NOT satisfied in 02 (Network bug sequence = 0, fixed here: sequence = s).</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>E&lt;&gt; Supervisor.Done</formula>
			<comment>Reachability: every drone can be armed and started.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>E&lt;&gt; Supervisor.Aborted</formula>
			<comment>Reachability: the command phase can abort. Expected: NOT satisfied when LOSSY = false (every mission is installed, so no command is ever denied), satisfied when LOSSY = true (Failed).</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>A[] (deadlock imply (Supervisor.Done || Supervisor.Aborted))</formula>
			<comment>The only blocking states are the two normal ends (no timelock, no blocked network).</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>A[] forall (i : drone_id) (armed[i] imply missionInstalled[i])</formula>
			<comment>Safety: no drone is armed without an installed mission.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>A[] forall (i : drone_id) (started[i] imply armed[i])</formula>
			<comment>Safety: no drone starts without being armed.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>A[] (Supervisor.Done imply forall (i : drone_id) started[i])</formula>
			<comment>Safety: the GCS reports success only if every drone really started.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>CommandClient(0).WaitAck --&gt; (CommandClient(0).Idle || CommandClient(0).Failed)</formula>
			<comment>Liveness: every command sent to drone 0 ends, with an answer or with Failed.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>Supervisor.Prepared --&gt; (Supervisor.Done || Supervisor.Aborted)</formula>
			<comment>Liveness: once the missions are uploaded, the command phase always ends.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>armed[0] --&gt; cmdAccepted[0][ARM]</formula>
			<comment>Liveness: if drone 0 is armed, the GCS eventually knows it. Expected: NOT satisfied when LOSSY = true (all the ACKs can be lost: a real limit of the protocol).</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>E&lt;&gt; CommandClient(0).Failed</formula>
			<comment>A command can fail after all its tries. Expected: NOT satisfied when LOSSY = false (ACK_TIMEOUT is long enough), satisfied when LOSSY = true.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>A[] forall (i : drone_id) forall (c : cmd_id) !(cmdAccepted[i][c] &amp;&amp; cmdFailed[i][c])</formula>
			<comment>Safety: the GCS never concludes both "accepted" and "failed" for the same command.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>E&lt;&gt; (cmdFailed[0][ARM] &amp;&amp; armed[0])</formula>
			<comment>The GCS can believe ARM failed while drone 0 is really armed (only the ACKs were lost). Expected: NOT satisfied when LOSSY = false, satisfied when LOSSY = true.</comment>
		</query>
		<query>
			<formula>sup{CommandClient(0).WaitAck} : CommandClient(0).x</formula>
			<comment>Measure: the longest time drone 0's client waits for an ACK. Must stay below ACK_TIMEOUT when LOSSY = false, otherwise the timeout fires for nothing.</comment>
		</query>
	</queries>
</nta>
